"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify A4-2's post-rollback STATE: assert what the reverted differ does when it reads key-set-only prev (self-heal vs mis-fire), and provide a data path (git-history recovery of full payloads, or a reverted-reader that tolerates key-set prev) — not merely a recorded reverse-diff artifact.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff recorded first.'","POST-ROLLBACK-STATE overlay trigger (d): A4-2 is a one-way transformation with no back-out that restores the discarded payloads.","Approach section documents the exact failure mode this risks: an empty/degenerate prev makes the differ 're-derive 2050+ inbound creates every pass'.","ABSENCE: the 'rollback artifact' is a diff record, not a mechanism restoring full-payload prev; no assertion of differ behavior post-revert against key-set-only prev."],"finding":"A4-2 (prev_snapshot -> key-set) is irreversible and its named rollback artifact is a reverse-direction corpus DIFF, which validates the forward change but is not a data-restoration path and does not describe the STATE after an A4-2 code revert. Once key-set prev is committed, the full ACLI payloads are absent from the worktree; a reverted differ that expects full-payload prev now runs against key-set-only prev.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f3ba30ffb598e79","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Compatibility and rollback: 'reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff recorded first'; scope item A4-2; AC line 'Corpus mutation-diff ... the reverse-direction diff is recorded as the A4-2 rollback artifact'","norm_id":"n81a83f159f00340a","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A4-2 ships and prev_snapshot is stored as a bare key-set; a defect forces reverting the A4-2 differ code, which now reads key-set prev where it expects full payloads and either crashes or re-derives thousands of spurious inbound creates against Jira."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC that a reverted (pre-A4-2) differ run against a key-set-only prev_snapshot produces zero spurious inbound creates (or define the recovery step that restores full-payload prev from history before the code revert), and attach a literal DATA LOSS RISK note that A4-2 discards the full ACLI payloads.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile A4-2 and A4-3: state one authoritative model of whether key-set-prev branch-3 mutations reach the apply loop (short-circuit at acli.py vs. suppressed by drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions before ctx.mutations), and make both children's rationale consistent with it.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["A4-2 (c872) 'Measured effect'/'Why this is safe': 'The feared _compute_mutations_emit_both field-clearing does not reach Jira: _mutation_to_batch_dict reads payload[\"changed_fields\"] ... so fields collapses to {} and update_issue(key) short-circuits at acli.py:181-185 with zero subprocess and zero network.'","A4-3 (02aa) 'Why': 'Each inert mutation still drives one per-mutation loop iteration in the batch apply path (applier.py:639-640), which calls _recheck_drift -> concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root) — a git rev-parse subprocess — before dispatching via _apply_one. So ~516 extra git invocations per pass ...'","A4-3 'Approach' then concludes those emissions are already removed by drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions in run_differs.py 'before ctx.mutations is set and before the apply loop can call _recheck_drift' — i.e. they never reach the apply loop at all.","container pairing: parent + 0232-1407-4600-415c/02aa-d30e-828a-4f21/03ef-28e6-58f3-425b/272e-9531-f392-468d/2b0a-4f32-8420-46c0/2d32-f685-6c5f-48d3/591f-2acd-dc28-448e/5ae0-411f-6d72-40f1/7ffa-c56b-22ef-4697/9738-b485-bb21-44ac/993a-33c3-87c0-4c16/c872-1ca4-584b-4314/f511-c542-58e4-48ca"],"finding":"A4-2 and A4-3 make conflicting assumptions about whether the key-set-prev branch-3 (outbound,update)/field_drift mutations reach the apply loop, so the two siblings encode contradictory models of the same code path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f281655e5444ce5fe","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 02aa-d30e-828a-4f21 (A4-3), cross-referenced with child c872-1ca4-584b-4314 (A4-2)","norm_id":"n3c210ee4425aea73","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A key-set prev routes ~516 both-present keys to _compute_mutations_emit_both in a production pass; a reader of A4-2 concludes the mutations are harmless-but-emitted (short-circuit at apply), while a reader of A4-3 concludes they are suppressed pre-apply — the two descriptions cannot both be the operative mechanism."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Pick the verified mechanism (source-inspect run_differs.py suppression order relative to ctx.mutations and the apply loop) and align both children's prose; if the run_differs suppression truly precedes apply, drop A4-2's acli.py short-circuit rationale as moot; if not, A4-3 must not claim the git-rev-parse path is already prevented.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/scripts/: 2b0a-4f32-8420-46c0 & 993a-33c3-87c0-4c16 (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 591f-2acd-dc28-448e & 7ffa-c56b-22ef-4697 (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 591f-2acd-dc28-448e & 9738-b485-bb21-44ac (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 591f-2acd-dc28-448e & f511-c542-58e4-48ca (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 7ffa-c56b-22ef-4697 & 9738-b485-bb21-44ac (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 7ffa-c56b-22ef-4697 & f511-c542-58e4-48ca (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py: 9738-b485-bb21-44ac & f511-c542-58e4-48ca (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_store/push.py: 272e-9531-f392-468d & 7ffa-c56b-22ef-4697 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","verify command `grep -r baseline_advanced_at src/` returns nothing.` greps the unanchored word 'baseline_advanced_at' — it substring-matches (e.g. 'review_baseline_advanced_at'); anchor it (\\b, ^$, or a quoted key like '\"baseline_advanced_at\":')","verify command `grep -r baseline_advanced_at src/` greps the unanchored word 'baseline_advanced_at' — it substring-matches (e.g. 'review_baseline_advanced_at'); anchor it (\\b, ^$, or a quoted key like '\"baseline_advanced_at\":')"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State A3's post-rollback behavior: assert (with a test) that the PRE-A3 reader interprets already-normalized-and-persisted baselines correctly, or make A3 write-back-compatible (normalize on read only, never persist) so rollback leaves no reader-incompatible state.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6933,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently.'","POST-ROLLBACK-STATE overlay trigger (a): A3 changes how existing persisted baseline records are interpreted (ADF dict vs normalized string).","ABSENCE: no assertion that the rolled-back (pre-A3) comparison path yields the correct verdict on baselines A3 already normalized-and-persisted."],"finding":"A3 (baseline text-normalization) is claimed reversible solely because 'the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently', but that guarantee describes the NEW reader. If A3 persists normalized-string baselines and the code is then rolled back, the plan does not assert the PRE-A3 reader correctly interprets the already-normalized (dict->string) baselines it finds in the store. Post-rollback the store holds normalized data the old comparison path never expected.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7260cb57588f280","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Compatibility and rollback: 'A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently'; scope item A3","norm_id":"nac7769ceb6c92313","priority":0.2567,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A3 ships, set_baseline writes normalized-string baselines for weeks, then A3 is reverted; the restored old reader compares a stored normalized string against a fresh dict-shaped Jira payload and mis-classifies the field as changed/unchanged, driving a spurious or suppressed Jira write."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC that the pre-A3 comparison path, fed a store containing A3-normalized baselines, yields the same verdict as against the original dict shape — or confine A3 normalization to the read/compare path so nothing reader-incompatible is ever persisted.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6933,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently' — the read path referenced is the new/normalizing one","POST-ROLLBACK overlay applies: A3 is an in-place reinterpretation of existing persisted records (baseline value shape), not a purely-additive optional field","The plan's reverse-direction rollback artifact is scoped to A4-2 only ('reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff'); no equivalent post-rollback interpretation assertion is recorded for A3's already-normalized residue"],"